-- title:
--   Local components of the lattice cut out by a finite idele
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a ring which is a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $D$ which is finitely generated and whose $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $D$. Write $\widehat{\Lambda} =$ [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda$ for the additive subgroup of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ generated by the elements $z \otimes a$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $a$ a finite adele all of whose components lie in the local integers, and, for a finite place $v$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ (a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$), write $\Lambda_v =$ [`Submodule.localBox`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) $\Lambda\, v$ for the additive subgroup of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the elements $z \otimes c$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of the completion at $v$. Let $g$ be a unit of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ and let $\Lambda^{g} =$ [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) $\Lambda\, g$ be the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\{d \in D : d \otimes 1 \in g \cdot \widehat{\Lambda}\}$ of $D$. Then for every $x \in D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$, one has $x \in (\Lambda^{g})_v$ if and only if there is a $y \in \Lambda_v$ with $x = g_v\, y$, where $g_v$ denotes the image of $g$ under the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map $\mathrm{id}_D \otimes (\text{evaluation at } v)$ from $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ to $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$.
--
--   This is one half of the local–global dictionary for lattices in a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra: the local component at $v$ of the lattice cut out in $D$ by a finite idele $g$ is the left translate by $g_v$ of the local component of $\Lambda$. It is used in the finite-idele (double coset) description of lattices and orders, in particular in the Čerednik–Drinfeld coset-graph computations identifying quotients of vertices and edges with class sets of Eichler orders.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Submodule_mem_localBox_ofFiniteIdele_iff.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox
import Definitions.Def_Submodule_LocalBox

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open scoped TensorProduct Pointwise
open IsDedekindDomain NumberField

theorem Submodule.mem_localBox_ofFiniteIdele_iff
    {D : Type*} [Ring D] [Algebra ℚ D] (Λ : Submodule ℤ D)
    (hfg : Λ.FG) (hsp : Submodule.span ℚ (Λ : Set D) = ⊤)
    (g : (D ⊗[ℚ] FiniteAdeleRing (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ)ˣ) (v : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 ℚ))
    (x : D ⊗[ℚ] v.adicCompletion ℚ) :
    x ∈ Submodule.localBox (Submodule.ofFiniteIdele Λ g) v ↔
      ∃ y ∈ Submodule.localBox Λ v,
        x = Submodule.finiteAdeleEvalAt D v (g : D ⊗[ℚ] FiniteAdeleRing (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ) * y := by sorry
